# Distributed PyTorch Training on 2 Nodes (Kathara)

This lab runs distributed training on 2 virtual machines connected over a shared collision domain (A), comparing DDP against manual weight synchronization at the end of each epoch[cite: 1, 2].

## 1. Dataset Setup

Place the pre-downloaded FashionMNIST dataset inside:
shared/data/FashionMNIST/raw/

Both machines access this data through the shared folder[cite: 1, 2]. DistributedSampler partitions 30,000 samples to each node[cite: 1, 2].

---

## 2. Start the Lab and Wireshark

From the host command prompt:

kathara lstart

Attach Wireshark to collision domain A:

kathara lconfig -n wireshark --add A

Open browser at:
http://localhost:3000

---

## 3. Network Emulation: Packet Loss (Optional for Study)

To simulate network degradation and observe TCP retransmissions during training, configure packet loss on pc2 before running any training option.

Enable 5% packet loss on pc2 (run inside pc2 terminal):
tc qdisc add dev eth0 root netem loss 5%

Verify that packet loss is active:
tc qdisc show dev eth0

Remove packet loss and restore normal network conditions (run inside pc2 terminal):
tc qdisc del dev eth0 root

---

## 4. Option A: Run DDP Training (Sync Every Batch)

On pc1 (Rank 0 - Master):
python3 /shared/Train_DDP.py 0

Immediately after, on pc2 (Rank 1):
python3 /shared/Train_DDP.py 1

---

## 5. Option B: Run Manual Sync Training (Sync at Epoch End)

On pc1 (Rank 0 - Master):
python3 /shared/Train_Sync_Manuale.py 0

Immediately after, on pc2 (Rank 1):
python3 /shared/Train_Sync_Manuale.py 1

Both scripts automatically track and print execution time, sent packets, and total transferred MB[cite: 1, 2].

---

## 6. Option C: Run Sync Every N Batches Training (Intermediate Approach)

The script accepts `<RANK>` and `<SYNC_EVERY>` (ex. sync every 10 batches)[cite: 1, 2]:

On pc1 (Rank 0 - Master):
python3 /shared/Train_Sync_N.py 0 10

Immediately after, on pc2 (Rank 1):
python3 /shared/Train_Sync_N.py 1 10

Weights are averaged every N batches and at the end of each epoch[cite: 1, 2]. The script prints execution time, sent packets, and total transferred MB[cite: 1, 2].

---

## 7. Stop the Lab

When execution finishes, shut down the lab from the host terminal:

kathara lclean
